{"id":"3cb5355dfd837c8e","group":"58","path":"58/batch20/58-thm-lebesgue-measurable-regularity.md","title":"Lebesgue Measurable Regularity","display":"thm-lebesgue-measurable-regularity — Lebesgue Measurable Regularity","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-lebesgue-measurable-regularity","aliases":["58-thm-lebesgue-measurable-regularity"],"display":"thm-lebesgue-measurable-regularity — Lebesgue Measurable Regularity","depends_on":["[[58-df-lebesgue]]","[[58-df-zfc-top5-open-set]]","[[../batch18/58-df-zfc-top2-compact-subset.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-lebesgue-measurable-regularity"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-lebesgue-measurable-regularity</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-lebesgue-measurable-regularity — Lebesgue Measurable Regularity"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"68427bc628af9b8d\" href=\"?note=68427bc628af9b8d\" title=\"58-df-lebesgue\">58-df-lebesgue</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"473439958a92cf5b\" href=\"?note=473439958a92cf5b\" title=\"58-df-zfc-top5-open-set\">58-df-zfc-top5-open-set</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"67cf48a2f6e27861\" href=\"?note=67cf48a2f6e27861\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-zfc-top2-compact-subset.md\">../batch18/58-df-zfc-top2-compact-subset.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A,K,O,\\lambda,\\mathcal L,\\tau_{\\mathbb R},\\varepsilon\\in V\">\\(A,K,O,\\lambda,\\mathcal L,\\tau_{\\mathbb R},\\varepsilon\\in V\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S(\\lambda,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)\">\\(\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S(\\lambda,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)\\)</span> is the exact measure predicate.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_{\\mathbb R}=\\{U\\in\\mathcal P(\\mathbb R):\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists r\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall y\\in\\mathbb R\\;(|x-y|&lt;r\\to y\\in U)\\}\">\\(\\tau_{\\mathbb R}=\\{U\\in\\mathcal P(\\mathbb R):\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists r\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall y\\in\\mathbb R\\;(|x-y|&lt;r\\to y\\in U)\\}\\)</span> is the usual Euclidean topology.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcTop5OpenSet}_S(\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathbb R},O)\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcTop5OpenSet}_S(\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathbb R},O)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcTop2CompactSubset}_S(K,\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathbb R})\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcTop2CompactSubset}_S(K,\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathbb R})\\)</span> type the approximants.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}lebesgue\\text{-}measurable\\text{-}regularity}\\vdash \\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S(\\lambda,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)\\land\\tau_{\\mathbb R}=\\{U\\in\\mathcal P(\\mathbb R):\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists r\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall y\\in\\mathbb R\\;(|x-y|&lt;r\\to y\\in U)\\}\\land A\\in\\mathcal L\\land\\lambda(A)&lt;\\infty\\land\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\to\\exists K,O\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\;\\left(\\mathrm{ZfcTop2CompactSubset}_S(K,\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathbb R})\\land\\mathrm{ZfcTop5OpenSet}_S(\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathbb R},O)\\land K\\subseteq A\\subseteq O\\land\\lambda(O\\setminus K)&lt;\\varepsilon\\right).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}lebesgue\\text{-}measurable\\text{-}regularity}\\vdash \\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S(\\lambda,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)\\land\\tau_{\\mathbb R}=\\{U\\in\\mathcal P(\\mathbb R):\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists r\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall y\\in\\mathbb R\\;(|x-y|&lt;r\\to y\\in U)\\}\\land A\\in\\mathcal L\\land\\lambda(A)&lt;\\infty\\land\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\to\\exists K,O\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\;\\left(\\mathrm{ZfcTop2CompactSubset}_S(K,\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathbb R})\\land\\mathrm{ZfcTop5OpenSet}_S(\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathbb R},O)\\land K\\subseteq A\\subseteq O\\land\\lambda(O\\setminus K)&lt;\\varepsilon\\right).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The topology parameter is fixed to the usual Euclidean topology; allowing an arbitrary topology would make the stated regularity theorem false.</li>\n<li>Lebesgue 可测集可以从外部用开集逼近</li>\n<li>可以分解为 Borel 集 + 零测集</li>\n<li>Lebesgue 测度在紧集上是内部正则的</li>\n<li>完备性：零测集的子集仍是 Lebesgue 可测的</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-lebesgue","status":"resolved","id":"68427bc628af9b8d","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-lebesgue]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-zfc-top5-open-set","status":"resolved","id":"473439958a92cf5b","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-zfc-top5-open-set]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch18/58-df-zfc-top2-compact-subset.md","status":"resolved","id":"67cf48a2f6e27861","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch18/58-df-zfc-top2-compact-subset.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"A,K,O,\\lambda,\\mathcal L,\\tau_{\\mathbb R},\\varepsilon\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S(\\lambda,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau_{\\mathbb R}=\\{U\\in\\mathcal P(\\mathbb R):\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists r\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\\forall y\\in\\mathbb R\\;(|x-y|<r\\to y\\in U)\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZfcTop5OpenSet}_S(\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathbb R},O)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZfcTop2CompactSubset}_S(K,\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathbb R})","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}lebesgue\\text{-}measurable\\text{-}regularity}\\vdash \\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S(\\lambda,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)\\land\\tau_{\\mathbb R}=\\{U\\in\\mathcal P(\\mathbb R):\\forall x\\in U\\;\\exists r\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\\forall y\\in\\mathbb R\\;(|x-y|<r\\to y\\in U)\\}\\land A\\in\\mathcal L\\land\\lambda(A)<\\infty\\land\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\to\\exists K,O\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\;\\left(\\mathrm{ZfcTop2CompactSubset}_S(K,\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathbb R})\\land\\mathrm{ZfcTop5OpenSet}_S(\\mathbb R,\\tau_{\\mathbb R},O)\\land K\\subseteq A\\subseteq O\\land\\lambda(O\\setminus K)<\\varepsilon\\right).","display":true}],"bytes":1881,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4277","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch20/58-thm-lebesgue-measurable-regularity.md|58-thm-lebesgue-measurable-regularity]]（batch20）"}],"outgoing":["68427bc628af9b8d","473439958a92cf5b","67cf48a2f6e27861"]}